# Docker build context excludes.
#
# Without this file the build context is the ENTIRE repo directory, which is
# shipped to the Docker daemon before the build starts. On a server install
# (e.g. Unraid /mnt/user/appdata) people copy a multi-GB backup into ./data
# before building — and since the Dockerfile never builds ./data into the image
# (it's bind-mounted at runtime: ./data/uploads:/data/uploads etc.), shipping it
# as build context just fills the Docker vDisk / cache and can hang the box.
# Excluding it keeps the context to source only (a few MB).

# Runtime data — bind-mounted at run time, NEVER part of the image.
data/
data
*.bak
*-backup
clipai-data-backup/
clipai-env-backup

# Version history + local tooling state.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.clipai/
.pytest_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo

# Frontend deps + build output (installed/built inside the image).
**/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/.vite/

# Companion build output — the image builds these itself (companion-builder
# stage); a stray local cargo/vite build here would ship GBs of context.
companion/dist/
companion/src-tauri/target/

# Secrets / env (provided at runtime via compose env_file / bind mount).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs, caches, scratch.
*.log
logs/
**/.DS_Store
*.tmp

# Media + model weights — large, fetched on demand into /data at runtime,
# never needed to build the image.
*.mp4
*.mkv
*.mov
*.webm
*.wav
*.pt
*.onnx
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
models/

# Tests + reference material aren't needed to build/run the service image.
reference/
